            <string>Remove the divergent (physically impossible) part of the velocity field inside the lumen, which reduces noise. Requires a lumen segmentation. Finite difference projection is the most accurate; divergence-free wavelet denoising also removes noise from the divergence-free part. Recommended before computing velocity derivatives (wall shear stress, pressure, vorticity).</string>
